{"start":"t:body","attrs":{}}
{"text":"\n      "}
{"start":"t:div","attrs":{"corresp":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shachar_avaqeshkha_gabirol","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n40.jpg"}}
{"text":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:p","attrs":{}}
{"start":"t:milestone","attrs":{"unit":"stanza","corresp":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shachar_avaqeshkha_gabirol_39123/1"}}
{"end":"t:milestone"}
{"tail":"In the morning I seek Thee, my rock and my fortress. I order my morning and also my evening prayer before Thee. "}
{"start":"t:milestone","attrs":{"unit":"stanza","corresp":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shachar_avaqeshkha_gabirol_39123/2"}}
{"end":"t:milestone"}
{"tail":"Before Thy grandeur I stand and tremble, for Thine eye sees all the thoughts of my heart. "}
{"start":"t:milestone","attrs":{"unit":"stanza","corresp":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shachar_avaqeshkha_gabirol_39123/3"}}
{"end":"t:milestone"}
{"tail":"What can heart and tongue accomplish, what can my strength, what can the spirit within me. "}
{"start":"t:milestone","attrs":{"unit":"stanza","corresp":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shachar_avaqeshkha_gabirol_39123/4"}}
{"end":"t:milestone"}
{"tail":"Behold, man’s song pleases Thee. Therefore, I wish to thank Thee as long as God’s breath is in me. "}
{"start":"t:milestone","attrs":{"unit":"stanza"}}
{"end":"t:milestone"}
{"end":"t:p"}
{"tail":"\n      "}
{"end":"t:div"}
{"tail":"\n    "}
{"end":"t:body"}
